---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/supplements';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'for/supplements');
const desc = description(site, 'for/supplements');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does structure/function wording make an email compliant?",
    "answer": "No automatic conclusion follows from that phrase. Review express and implied claims, supporting evidence and the overall message for the intended market."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should days of supply be calculated?",
    "answer": "Use package quantity and the approved label basis as an uncertain planning estimate, not individualized dosing advice. Account for multiple bottles, delayed delivery and current subscription state."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should another supplement be recommended?",
    "answer": "Only through product-specific reviewed merchandising with a qualified route for suitability or interaction questions. A fixed post-purchase delay does not establish compatibility."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can an email tool certify compliance?",
    "answer": "This guide establishes no such certification. Require review controls and version management, then obtain product and market-specific review separately."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/for">All store types</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Supplement email: choose for reviewed claims and careful reorder timing</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">A supplement email program needs product-specific review, reliable subscription state and conservative stock estimates. An automation template cannot certify a health claim or determine how a customer should use a product.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Set a claims-review boundary</h2>
    <p>For US advertising, the FTC Health Products Compliance Guidance explains that express and implied health claims need adequate substantiation before dissemination. Calling copy education or using structure/function phrasing does not remove the need to assess its overall impression. The guidance is not a safe harbor. This is a scoped US advertising reference, not clearance for a product, labeling, privacy, consent or another jurisdiction.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Build a versioned product-copy library</h2>
    <p>Record the approved product wording, supporting evidence owner, intended market, review date and where each block is used. Include subject lines, testimonials, images and linked landing pages in review; a cautious paragraph can still sit inside a misleading overall message. When a formulation or claim changes, find and pause affected scheduled flows until the responsible reviewer approves the replacement.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Estimate stock without prescribing use</h2>
    <p>Use the actual SKU package quantity and its approved label basis. An explicitly hypothetical arithmetic example: 60 units divided by an assumed two units per day equals 30 days of supply. That assumption is not dosing advice or a predicted customer outcome. Delivery delays, irregular use and spare bottles change reminder timing. Ask whether a reorder is useful rather than telling customers to increase use or combine products.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Keep subscriptions and safety inquiries out of sales pressure</h2>
    <p>Use current contract state to exclude active recurring deliveries from duplicate reorder campaigns. Re-evaluate after pause, skip, refund or product change. Route adverse-experience or interaction questions to the merchant designated qualified support process. Suppress promotional cross-sell while a relevant issue is unresolved; email segmentation cannot decide compatibility or individual suitability.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Design onboarding around the purchased item</h2>
    <p>Offer access to approved label information, ingredient details and support for the exact formulation. Do not promise that a habit forms on a particular day or schedule a universal complementary-product bundle. Keep practitioner or wholesale follow-up separate from consumer replenishment so account discussions and product-use questions reach their proper owners.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Demonstration brief and proposed review rehearsal</h2>
    <p>Ask Sequenzy and other candidates to show copy-version replacement across live flows, review permissions, SKU-level stock estimates and subscription suppression using your actual integration. These are proposed tests, not verified features or results. Rehearse a formulation update, paused contract, delayed shipment and unresolved product inquiry before enabling a reminder.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify">
    <h2>Measure repeat demand with review controls</h2>
    <p>Separate one-time reorder from contracted deliveries and refunded orders. Report review coverage, time to withdraw outdated claims, support escalations and opt-outs alongside contribution from eligible repeat purchases. A passed internal checklist is an operational record, not legal certification. Product-specific substantiation and market review remain the merchant responsibility.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2>Service ownership and evidence</h2>
    <p><a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/fulfillment/setup/notifications">Shopify store notifications</a> documents event-based order, fulfillment, refund, exchange and account notices. Assign each service event a sender before adding marketing automation; this source does not verify any third-party integration. Reviewed 24 November 2026.</p>
    <p>US advertising reference: <a class="link" href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/health-products-compliance-guidance">FTC Health Products Compliance Guidance</a>, reviewed 24 November 2026. Product and market-specific legal review remains unresolved by this guide.</p>
    <p><a class="link" href="/apps">Tool catalog</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/replenishment">Replenishment workflow</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/product-launch">Product launch workflow</a></p>
  </div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
